WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.049
Code review for XSS prevention should follow data into browser contexts.

2
00:00:04.049 --> 00:00:11.885
Reviewers can ask where untrusted data enters, where it is stored, which
templates or API responses expose it, and how the frontend renders it.

3
00:00:11.885 --> 00:00:24.750
Useful review focuses include unsafe rendering shortcuts, disabled
escaping, raw HTML insertion, unreviewed template filters, rich-content
handling, URL construction, error pages, admin screens, and client-side
DOM updates.

4
00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:30.757
Tests should verify escaping and sanitization behavior for the fields and
rendering paths that matter most.

5
00:00:30.757 --> 00:00:42.512
Unit and integration tests can check that known risky fields remain text,
that rich-content policies preserve allowed formatting while removing
unsafe content, and that templates continue using safe defaults.

6
00:00:42.512 --> 00:00:51.197
Regression tests are especially useful after template refactors, frontend
rewrites, sanitization library updates, or changes in how API data is
rendered.

7
00:00:51.197 --> 00:01:00.535
Logging should support investigation without collecting unnecessary
browser-side secrets, credentials, tokens, session data, or sensitive
personal information.

8
00:01:00.535 --> 00:01:08.568
Client-side errors and CSP reports can help identify rendering problems,
but they should be handled as potentially sensitive operational data.

9
00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:17.057
Monitoring unusual client-side errors or policy reports can reveal broken
rendering paths, misconfigured defenses, or unexpected frontend behavior.

10
00:01:17.057 --> 00:01:22.020
Remediation should address the root rendering path rather than only the
visible symptom.

11
00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:34.623
That may mean restoring autoescaping, replacing unsafe raw insertion,
adding a content policy, re-sanitizing stored content, narrowing API
responses, updating tests, or reviewing related templates that use the
same helper.

12
00:01:34.623 --> 00:01:41.480
XSS prevention requires continuous review because templates, APIs,
frontend code, and content policies change over time.
